    "ui.conflict_elsewhere": "Not saved: layout.json was changed somewhere else in the meantime. What is on this screen is still here.",
    "ui.conflict_mismatch": "Careful: the file does not contain what is shown here. Please check the text and report it - this is a bug in the program.",
    "ui.credits_metacom": "Symbols: METACOM 9 (Annette Kitzinger), licensed for this computer - they are only referenced, not copied into the project.",
    "ui.device_size": "this big on the device",
    "ui.dsg_arasaac": "When a pictogram is searched for, your browser sends the search word to the public interface of arasaac.org (Government of Aragon, Spain) and loads the pictures it finds from there. Your IP address is transmitted as a technical necessity. Whole sentences are not transmitted. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR - without that request there are no symbols. Spain is in the EU, so there is no transfer to a third country.",
    "ui.dsg_arasaac_head": "Searching ARASAAC",
    "ui.dsg_azure": "If you store an Azure key of your own, the sentence to be spoken is sent to Microsoft's speech service and comes back as sound. This is the only path on which something you typed leaves this computer, and it is off out of the box. Microsoft is the controller for the processing there, towards you as the holder of the account; the legal basis here is your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, which you can withdraw at any time by removing the key. The key itself stays in your browser.",
    "ui.dsg_azure_head": "Azure voices, only with a key of your own",
    "ui.dsg_cdn": "So that speech can be computed in the browser, the page loads the onnxruntime-web runtime from the public jsDelivr network (Prospect One, Krakow, Poland) the first time something is spoken. Your IP address is transmitted, no content. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.",
    "ui.dsg_cdn_head": "A library from jsDelivr",
    "ui.dsg_controller": "Stefanie Grewenig\nTalheide 5\n21149 Hamburg\nGermany",
    "ui.dsg_controller_head": "Controller",
    "ui.dsg_device": "The talker gets its contents over the USB cable, straight from this page. No network is involved: nothing goes to the internet, nothing comes to me, and the device has no Wi-Fi any more.",
    "ui.dsg_device_head": "The device",
    "ui.dsg_hosting": "The page is served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). On each request GitHub processes technically necessary access data, among them your IP address, the time, the file requested and your browser identification. I have no access to it and receive no statistics. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR - the legitimate interest in being able to serve the page at all. The transfer to the USA rests on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, under which GitHub is certified.",
    "ui.dsg_hosting_head": "Hosting and server logs",
    "ui.dsg_lead": "vorlaut runs entirely in your browser. There is no server, there are no accounts, no analytics and no advertising. Your sets, your sentences and your METACOM files do not leave your computer - I cannot see them, not even if asked.",
    "ui.dsg_none": "No analytics or tracking services, no advertising networks, no social media plugins, no fonts from other people's servers, no passing of data to third parties, no automated decision-making or profiling.",
    "ui.dsg_none_head": "What does not happen",
    "ui.dsg_rights": "You have the rights of access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and objection (Art. 21 GDPR). As I hold no personal data of yours, a request for access will usually come back empty. You may complain to any supervisory authority; the one responsible for me is the Hamburg Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information.",
    "ui.dsg_rights_head": "Your rights",
    "ui.dsg_stand": "Last updated: August 2026",
    "ui.dsg_storage": "Your sets, sentences, pictures, settings, the Azure key, the voice models you fetched and the link to your METACOM folder live in your browser's local database (IndexedDB and OPFS). They stay there until you delete them - through the browser's own function for clearing website data. This storage is strictly necessary for the function you explicitly asked for and therefore needs no consent under § 25(2)(2) TDDDG. That is also why there is no cookie banner here: there is nothing one would be needed for.",
    "ui.dsg_storage_head": "Storage on your device",
    "ui.dsg_voices": "The offline voices are Piper models and are fetched from huggingface.co when needed (Hugging Face, Inc., USA) - about 63 MB per voice, once. Your IP address is transmitted, no content; after that speech needs no network at all. This only happens once you fetch voices or pick one - the legal basis is your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. The models then live in your browser.",
    "ui.dsg_voices_head": "Voices from Hugging Face",
